# Copy to config.env and edit. Every setting has a working default, so an empty
# config.env (or none at all) is fine for a first run on a Mac with 48 GB or
# more. With less, set LLM_MODEL.
#
# config.env is gitignored.

# The macOS account that runs the model server and owns its API key. Defaults to
# whoever runs the scripts (or ran `sudo`). The server runs while this account
# is logged in.
#LLM_USER=

# The model, as Splash's --model takes it: an MLX repository, or a GGUF
# repository and variant, OWNER/REPO:VARIANT (for example
# unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF:UD-Q2_K_XL). The default needs 48 GB or more:
# on a Mac with less, set this before the first run (README.md, "Models").
# Splash downloads the model at its first start and pairs its draft model by
# itself. It is also the model ID clients use, so changing it means changing
# every client's config.
#LLM_MODEL=mlx-community/Qwen3.8-27B-4bit

# Empty, the default: the machine joins the tailnet as one of your devices,
# which config/tailscale-policy.hujson grants. Set a tag, such as
# tag:llm-server, to join as a tagged device instead, and follow the comment at
# the end of the policy file.
#LLM_TAG=

# The tailnet HTTPS port `tailscale serve` publishes the endpoint on. Change it
# to keep 443 free for something else on this Mac, such as 8443.
#LLM_HTTPS_PORT=443

# Laptops only. "yes" runs `pmset -a disablesleep 1`, which keeps a laptop
# serving with the lid shut. It is system-wide, battery included, and
# undocumented in `man pmset`. Verified on mains power only (README, step 6).
# With it, a watchdog shuts the Mac down cleanly on battery at
# LLM_BATTERY_SHUTDOWN_PCT percent, instead of running flat.
#LLM_DISABLE_SLEEP=no
#LLM_BATTERY_SHUTDOWN_PCT=15
